WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.520
And so, let's all have a listen.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.270
Dear Hell...

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.570
Jigoku mitai ni asobitai
I want to have a good time like Hell

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.700
Jigoku mitai ni yasumitai
I want to rest like Hell

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.540
Jigoku mitai na nidoneshite
I want to go back to sleep like Hell

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.130
Teiji de agaritai
And finish work on time

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.970
Jigoku mitai ni tabesugite
I ate too much like Hell

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.720
Jigoku mitai ni nomisugita
I drank too much like Hell

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.980
Aa sonna wake de
Ah, for these reasons

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.230
Jigoku mitai
It's like Hell

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.650
Sonna toki koso deban desu
At such a time it's all the more his turn on stage

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.320
Hoozuki-sama ga moriageru
Mr. Hozuki livens things up

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.410
Omakase kudasai!
Please leave it to me!

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:03.000
Aa jigoku jigoku mainichi jigoku
Ah, Hell, Hell, every day Hell

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.580
Jigoku jigoku
Hell, Hell

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.250
"Uso desho?!"
"You can't mean that, right?!"

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:13.170
Jigoku jigoku youkoso jigoku
Hell, Hell, welcome to Hell

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.010
Atchi muite
Look that way

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:14.590
Kotchi muite
Look this way

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.720
Abikyoukan!
Pandemonium!

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.090
Gongo! Doudan!
What the hell!

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.890
Shitsureishimashita!
Pardon me!

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:23.890
Sonna kanji no
In that kind of way

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:27.980
A! Jigoku desu! Jajajajan!
Ah! It's Hell! Ta ta ta-da!

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:28.980
Katsu!
Curses!

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.070
DANGER
NO SWIMMING

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.370
The Stripping Hag and Clothes-Hanging Geezer

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.340
DANGER
NO SWIMMING

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:49.080
Swim, swim, swim...

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.340
Hey, you guys! The sign says "no swimming," you know!

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:55.550
Hurry and get on out!

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:59.640
Hey! Get outta there!

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:57.720
STOMP
STOMP
STOMP
STOMP

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.100
Stupid dog! Idiot monkey!

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.100
Gaaah! It's the Mountain Hag!

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.810
I'm sorry! We didn't know!

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:09.190
You one of their buddies?! I'll cut your tongue off!

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:09.810
That's some amazing strength for an old hag!

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.110
Rurio!
That's some amazing strength for an old hag!

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:12.770
What's the matter here?

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.110
Mr. Hozuki!

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.650
She's so scary!

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:21.070
She's been nicknamed "Blah-Blah Hag" by the local kids.
She's one of those scary old grannies!

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:27.040
Well, it is true that the kids in Children's Limbo
were calling her "Booby Hag."

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.080
What's this? You should've just told me you were
Mr. Hozuki's dog in the first place, Doggy.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:36.130
Yuck! The old hag's acting
like a regular woman all of a sudden!

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.010
Shh!

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:40.510
Please realize that women never cease
to see themselves as women no matter their age.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.260
You'll save yourself a lot of trouble that way.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:45.810
Wasn't that a pretty awful thing to say about her?

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.350
Well, who is she anyway?

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.440
She's the Stripping Hag.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.650
Ah, so she's the one...

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.190
If I remember correctly...

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:58.240
* This image is for illustrative purposes only.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:56.400
there's also an old man called
the Clothes-Hanging Geezer, right?

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.400
The one who's the husband of the Stripping Hag.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:00.360
You really know your stuff.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.990
I mean, in the Mundane World,
reference materials sometimes don't even list him.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:07.750
Right now... he's over on the opposite bank.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.660
HERE

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.500
Wow...

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.540
What jobs do those two do exactly?

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.380
They do a rough weighing of the deceased's sins,
plus they act as lookouts.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:21.470
YUKYOTO
SANSUISE
KOSHINEN

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:21.590
The Sanzu River is crossed over by the dead at
different points depending on the gravity of their sins.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.050
YUKYOTO
GOOD PEOPLE
SANSUISE
KOSHINEN

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:25.350
Good people cross over a bridge called Yukyoto.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:28.430
YUKYOTO
GOOD PEOPLE
SANSUISE
PEOPLE WITH
MINOR SINS

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:28.430
KOSHINEN

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.770
Those with minor sins cross
at some shallows called Sansuise.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:33.270
YUKYOTO
GOOD PEOPLE
SANSUISE
PEOPLE WITH
MINOR SINS
KOSHINEN
PEOPLE WITH
GRAVE SINS

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.100
Those with grave sins cross
at a deep spot called Koshinen.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:37.780
KANEI TSUHO (COPPER COIN)

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:37.940
The six Mon coins the bereaved family gives the
deceased in order to avoid the suffering of the crossing

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.940
are considered part of the memorial service.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:45.030
YUKYOTO
SANSUISE
THE DECEASED
KOSHINEN

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:44.490
It is the Stripping Hag who decides
where the deceased will make the crossing.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.910
When the clothes of the dead
are hung on an Eryoju Tree,

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.210
its branches sag in accordance
with the gravity of their sins.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.830
She then evaluates how much they're sagging.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.540
I'll have you cross at Koshinen.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:01.300
By the way, it is at this time that the
Hell-supplied clothes of the dead are passed out.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.300
Wow...

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.050
So the dead have all changed into new clothes, huh?

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:08.350
Not everyone is necessarily
wearing the same clothing when they die, after all.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:11.060
When they cross the river,
the Clothes-Hanging Geezer is waiting.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.600
The clothes are now hung on
an Eryoju Tree on this side of the river,

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:18.650
and the amount of water they absorbed is measured,
allowing him to see where the deceased crossed from.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.780
Then, the dead head to see King Shoko,
who acts as the river's administrator.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:30.040
KING SHOKO
SECOND
WEEK
MEMORIAL

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.950
There a trial is held, which includes them
giving a proper, falsehood-free account

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.410
of how they crossed just where they were supposed to.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.910
And that concludes my explanation
of the Sanzu River's significance.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.170
So this river's so dangerous
it presents an ordeal for the dead, huh?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.300
Right, and that's why swimming's prohibited.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.130
Allow me to introduce you...

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.850
The master of the Sanzu River...

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.150
and the monster crab.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.570
G-grim stuff...

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.900
And there are others besides them...

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:16.540
This is a mermaid family. They drown people.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.290
They sure don't look like blood relatives to me...

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.630
Are there any mermen?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:23.970
There are indeed.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.590
FROM AN EDO PERIOD
TITLE BLOCK PRINT
MERMAN
ILLUSTRATION

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:27.970
Doesn't look very tasty...

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.010
Miss, I bet you're tasty, though! Your meat, I mean!

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:31.760
Gah!

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:36.980
Well, before thinking about whether it would be tasty
or not, realize you're talking about mermaid meat.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.150
A price of 10 million yen for 100 grams
is actually on the cheap end.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.320
Brings to mind that
Eight Hundred-Year-Old Buddhist Priestess...

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:47.320
I see. If someone eats you,
it'll have an anti-aging effect on them.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:50.160
It's 'cause we were overfished so much
that I decided to move down here in the first place!

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.710
We have kappa and the soaked woman here, too.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:59.710
They're mostly here for the purpose of attacking
the dead who cross at Koshinen, you see.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:05.260
Quite thorough that the dead must contend
with ordeals in Hell while their trials are still ongoing...

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.590
Hey, so your husband, the Clothes-Hanging Geezer,

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:12.720
doesn't get mad when you blatantly flatter
Mr. Hozuki and other men?

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.140
You'll understand if you meet him.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:19.060
Cross over this bridge and try seeing
the old geezer for yourself.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:29.110
Who're you guys? You don't seem
to be members of the dead...

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.910
As his wife, you don't mind that?

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.870
He's always been like that.
A real good-for-nothing, isn't he?

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.710
Well, seems a bunch of the dead have gathered.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:43.460
Hey, line up! Those of you with six Mon coins,
get in this line here.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.800
She didn't waste any time
getting down to business, huh?

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.340
One way or another, I can sense she's a veteran.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.510
Hey, Old Hag!

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:56.350
What do you want, Geezer? Lots of the dead
are about to head over there, so get ready to wor-

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:59.190
I'm heading out now for a bit
to go watch the Maki-Miki concert.

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:00.850
You gotta be kidding!

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:01.600
She's fast!

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.860
She's not gonna chase down the old man?

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.820
If they're not breaking up over this,
maybe - in a certain way - they're quite close.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:11.910
He's always making me head to the far bank and work
both jobs at once, that good-for-nothing geezer!

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.620
That geezer's such an old-timer,
it's difficult to fire him, you know?

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:21.290
Isn't that why he's disappeared from
the reference materials in the Mundane World?

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:25.590
Probably also the reason there
are a variety of rumors about the old woman.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.260
MR. HOZUKI!

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:33.050
Is it really true that you're one of Maki's acquaintances?!

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.550
Get her autograph for me! That's not a problem, right?!

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.140
I'd like one from Miki, too!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.980
I staunchly refuse.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:42.440
For mercy's sake, get me an autograph!

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.520
For the time being, you should be focusing
on offering an apology to the Stripping Hag.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.820
If you want to make any requests,
put in some effort and earn your salary first, please.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:52.150
DON'T BE SO ARGUMENTATIVE!
I'm an old-timer, you know!

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.990
Why didn't you tell me about it?!

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:59.080
The fact that you didn't know Maki-Miki
appeared in a Hell PR campaign

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:02.670
means that you don't look at any of the information
coming out of the Offices of the Ten Kings.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:06.340
How about I give you the dismissal you've
so long desired on the grounds of neglect of your duties?

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:08.840
Not a chance! I'll resolutely remain at my post.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:12.090
I'm not gonna quit so easily, you know.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:15.760
I'll get a golden parachute! I'll get my money!

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:19.270
Way to run your mouth right in front of the top guy
at the Personnel Department, Gramps.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:24.400
Conversely, you sure it would work out for you?
Firing one of Sanzu River's most popular figures, I mean!

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.980
Popular figure
of Sanzu River
Clothes-Hanging
Geezer!!

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:28.320
The Stripping Hag is dozens of times more famous
than you, so, yeah, pretty much fine with me.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:34.070
Just how long has this old man remained at his post?

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:39.080
Well, you see, he's an old-timer who's been here
ever since Izanami was the chief of staff.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:41.870
At the time he actually worked hard at his job,

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.960
but the Stripping Hag is the kind of person
who finds one way or another to get things done,

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:47.040
so he began to seriously slack off.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:50.380
That geezer really is the worst...

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:55.510
What kind of official happily accepts his officer's
compensation, then doesn't even show up to work?

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.970
Say whatever you want... I don't care!

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:00.810
There's no other place of employment
as good as the one I've got.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.350
So he's not gonna quit no matter
how much he's criticized...

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:06.230
Is this the reason you said he's difficult to fire?

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:09.980
Why don't you just forcibly dismiss him?

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:13.740
Well, thing is, there are lots of thorny issues
when it comes to old-timers.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:18.200
Hanging clothes is a technical job,
and hiring a replacement is difficult, you know?

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:24.750
So it would be nice if he earnestly trained
the next generation, but he has zero willingness to do so.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:29.290
More importantly, come on and get me Maki's autograph
already! I'll do absolutely anything for it!

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:35.470
In that case, I'll ask for her autograph,
so will you teach me the technique for hanging clothes?

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.510
Not a chance!

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:42.770
He's quite cunning, isn't he?
He knows that if he teaches you his craft, Hozuki,

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:46.560
in the end he'll be fired
and won't be able to do a thing about it.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:50.110
Anyway, I'm begging you,
so just a single autograph, okay?! A single one!

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:51.860
I'M COUNTING ON YOU!

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:54.570
He ran off! Wait a second, you heartless old man!

00:09:54.820 --> 00:10:00.490
Absolutely terrifying... He's an active, negligent geezer
that even Mr. Hozuki has trouble handling.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.580
That sure is tough.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:09.920
Well, meow, it's purrty amazing he would
so proudly declare his self-centeredness.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:13.340
And yet "Clothes-Hanging Geezer" seems like a name
fit for an elderly gentleman, you know?

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:17.840
An elderly gentleman would be
someone like King Byodo.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:22.010
Whereas King Byodo dresses up like this
when he heads out,

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:26.140
the Clothes-Hanging Geezer heads out to concerts
while dressed like this despite being on duty.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.940
I feel kinda bad about that!

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:30.770
Maki, I get the sense you've been hurt just meow!

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:36.320
When a woman throws on an outer garment,
King Byodo is the type to nonchalantly lend a hand.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:36.530
Are you
alright?
Sorry to
trouble you

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.860
What a gentleman!

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:43.660
The Clothes-Hanging Geezer needs to hang up the
clothes of the dead on branches, but he simply doesn't.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.370
Feeling kinda tired,
so I'm leaving my duties
to the Old Hag today.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:44.830
Hey, now, Geezer!

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:47.500
That's the way everything is with him.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.750
The more I hear, the more I think it's hopeless.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.630
Well, a simple autograph is no problem.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:54.090
Where do you want me to write it?

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.630
Please autograph here... no problem if it's small.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:00.970
Also, in large print can you write "Let's retire!" for me?

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:04.760
I feel like sometime in the future
I might get sued over that, so I refuse.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.680
It would be nice if my autograph
is enough to get him to work.

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:10.100
That's just it.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:17.070
Do you really think I'm going to quietly head home
with only your autograph, Maki?

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.280
The Stripping Hag's First Nude Photo Book
The Forbidden Naked Form

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:22.070
FIRST
SHOW

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:23.370
I got her autograph for you.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.370
Why'd you have her autograph this thing?!

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:28.290
I actually had her sign one more thing.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:32.000
Marriage Registration
Name of the Husband                     Name of the Wife
Hozuki                                           Makibi
Hell's Offices of Enma                  Hell's Offices of Enma
Husband's Occupation: Chief of Staff      Wife's Occupation: Entertainer
Husband: Hozuki                                Wife: Makibi

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:32.170
If you don't work, I'm going to stamp this with my seal.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:33.830
What kinda threat is that?!

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.250
You're a real idiot, Mr. Hozuki!

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.550
If you dangle that in front of a fan,
of course they'll snatch it any cost!

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:40.760
Just try to take it!

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:44.050
Fork it over! Come on and give it here! Give it! Give it!

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:48.020
What're they doing messing around
with such an important official document? Those guys...
Fork it over! Come on and give it here! Give it! Give it!

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.270
You threaten Maki into signing that?!

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:52.650
I received permission from her management company.

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:56.440
Maki, there's not even a whiff
of romantic gossip surrounding you,

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.150
so I say go ahead and create a scandal.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:00.280
Show business is getting more and more degenerate!

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.530
I'll leak the story to the Nekomata Company!

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:06.370
That's just fine... so long as you don't mind
Maki getting wrapped in a scandal.

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:07.160
Damn it!

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:09.950
If you don't work, I'm going to sign those papers.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:12.790
I'll sign them even if you squeal
to the Nekomata Company.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:14.540
So, what's it gonna be?

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.500
Being threatened with divorce papers
is a common occurrence,

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:20.260
but what's the deal with being threatened
with marriage registration papers?!

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.970
You'll make enemies of Maki-Miki's entire fan base!

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:27.050
More than an attack from all their fans, I'm concerned
with improving your attitude toward your job!

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:28.970
Wh-what did you say?!

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.890
That was actually pretty cool!

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:36.480
Damn it... You've got me beat.
I've been defeated by your spirit.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:38.480
Not that I really get it...

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:40.480
Was he actually defeated?

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.030
If you take that to mean "he didn't win," then I'd say so.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:46.450
I'll do my job... for Maki's sake, that is!

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:47.780
Whoa...

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.370
It's surprising that Maki entrusted you with those papers.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.910
This is just a copy.

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:57.290
Maki has the actual documents, so I'm not in a position
where I could do something even if I wanted to.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:00.380
Besides, it would be bad if there was actually a scandal.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:04.510
If that happened, I'd just have Koban
write about the full truth of the story.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:09.050
In that case, the Clothes-Hanging Geezer
is the one who'd come out looking bad.

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:13.640
Well, if he's never even once taught a painful lesson,
I'd feel sorry for the Stripping Hag.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:18.730
No, the Stripping Hag isn't such a pushover
that you should feel sorry for her.

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.110
What's his deal?!

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:24.190
He actually had a copy of my photo book?

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:24.860
Huh?

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:26.450
The Stripping Hag's First Nude Photo Book
The Forbidden Naked Form
FIRST
SHOW

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:29.410
What's this autograph here? Whose is it?

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.740
Come on, write it properly.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.870
STRIPPING
HAG

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:36.290
She's a demon.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:40.380
Hello, Maki, thank you for your help.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:43.380
It's alright if you dispose of those papers now.

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:45.720
My manager took them from me...

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:50.100
I'm not sure what that guy's going to use them for,
so will you punish him for me?

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:52.010
We've got a demon right here...

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:55.640
The saying "Demons lurk at every corner"
really describes Hell, you know?

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:59.100
Well, demons are the main inhabitants, after all.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:07.200
It's strange... I mean, I looked at the recipe book and
took my time to understand everything when I made this.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:13.160
I'll have my older brothers see how it tastes.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.000
Yakankan

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.040
It's delicious.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:27.090
He's trying not to hurt my feelings...
That king of equivocation...

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.260
Pretty odd taste, isn't it?

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:31.010
That's just the kinda recipe it is, right?

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:35.270
I mean, the first time we ate avocado,
we didn't get the appeal, you know?

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:39.520
Guess there is something a bit different about
the stuff a smart person cooks, after all.

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:47.740
Chef Miki

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:49.990
Quagmire Television

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.820
Quagmire Music
Gogo With Hell!

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.820
Greenroom 2
Maki-Miki

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:54.790
Good meowning to you!

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:56.910
Good morning!

00:14:57.370 --> 00:15:00.960
Maki, most of the time, you don't bring
a bento for your on-location meal, huh?

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.210
Do you make your own?

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.500
That's right! I wouldn't want to carelessly
eat too much and put on weight, after all...

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:07.510
So, what about today's?

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:10.630
Today, I attempted to make a character-themed bento!

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.100
A s-shinkuchu...?

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:19.020
My management company told me to post about
a character-themed bento on my blog, you see.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:21.480
But it was only after making it that I realized...

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:23.810
This bento is gross...

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:26.280
Yeah...

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:30.950
Really thinking about it,
I don't even like bugs much in the first place...

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:34.410
Why didn't you realize how it would end up
as you were making it?

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.830
I didn't have many ingredients
and I thought I could pull it off somehow...

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:40.620
But, these rolled eggs look purrty good at least.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.210
And the spinach isn't all frazzled-looking.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.040
The asparagus look nice, too.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.170
What's with you all of a sudden?

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:50.470
Well, you see...

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:53.010
Huh?! Cooking?

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:57.560
Miki, I thought you were the kinda girl
who could do everything better than me!

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.100
Meow, that's obviously not the case!

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:02.770
Miki, you're knowledgeable, and you easily solve
math problems that come up on quiz shows,

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:05.770
I thought a Fairy from Study Land
was good at everything!

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:07.270
No one's good at every...

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.740
"A Fairy from Study Land"?!

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:08.980
One of
Study Land's

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:09.990
One of
Study Land's
Fairies?!

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:14.280
That's right! Somewhere in the world,
there's a place called Study Land,

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:17.740
and all the smart people are actually fairies from there...

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.580
Believing that made things...

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.120
...easier.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.630
What kinda self-defense mechanism is that...?

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:29.960
Which is why it came as a surprise
that you want me to teach you how to cook, Miki.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.800
Purrty please, help me out!

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:40.310
Ehhehehe
Tee-hee-hee-hee
Ehehehe
Hahahahaha

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:35.800
Seems she feels embarrassed...

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:37.850
Must be pretty darn happy...

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:40.430
I feel like I've done something good here.

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:45.310
In any event, I'd at least like to get good enough
that my cooking doesn't stand out as badly.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:46.060
If I don't...

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.020
Hell's
Cooking Queen
Championship

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:51.110
the issue will surely get exaggerated 10 times over
and I'll be made to appear on one of THOSE shows!

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:50.820
Hell's
Cooking Queen
Championship

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.400
Then, I'm already being treated as an idiot...

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:59.830
With my idiosyncratic personality as the main
selling point, I appear on various TV shows of that sort.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:02.750
That kind of thing is just part of the job.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.460
My apawlogies...

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:15.300
Archival Footage

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:08.960
But, Miki, when we filmed the Hell PR video,

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:12.050
you did just fine sharpening the knife
and stirring the pot, right?

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:15.510
Well, I'm capable of doing stuff
when I get told exactly what do to.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:20.470
The problem is, that no matter what I do,
I mess up with the seasoning and amount of heat.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:18.640
Pepper
Vinegar
Salt

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:24.310
Also, my impression of fish is that
they're something you can eat whole,

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:27.100
so I'm not actually good at preparing them.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:31.780
When I try to fillet them, they end up tattered
like one of the dead who's been subjected to torture.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.990
You've reminded me of a certain chief of staff
with a barbaric face!

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:38.410
So, just how should we go about cooking?

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:40.990
Wh-why are you here?!

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:44.410
Animals, if nothing else, are good at being threatening...

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:48.040
I saw your names on the door of the greenroom,
so I came to say hello.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:51.250
Wow, it's Maki-Miki! Give me an autograph, please!

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:56.880
This is a Hell minion named Shiro.
He's a guest of News Marvelous.

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:00.890
He achieved popularity after his appearance
in the PR video we made at the Offices of Enma.

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:03.390
Ah, I've seen that before.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.230
Yeah, I'm Shiro, Miki!

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:09.230
It's alright. I won't say anything about your cooking!

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:10.440
You heard us talking?!

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.070
He's a dog, so of course, he has good hearing.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:17.150
But, from what I've heard,
it shouldn't be that big of a deal, right?

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:20.280
So long as in the future you can find yourself
a husband who can cook.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:24.540
Please don't give me suggestions based
on summarized hearsay of what someone overheard!

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.000
What will I do if my husband catches a cold?

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.290
And if all the restaurants are closed?

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.630
I'd be in a purrty big bind if that happened.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:34.090
It'll be fine!

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:38.510
I'm sure seeing you so concerned about him
would be enough to make him happy.

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.800
That sort of kindness is a precious thing.

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:45.390
My senpai's wife is more uncompromising than that,
but he seems happy.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.480
The one who persists to the end is the winner!

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:50.560
Shiro, sometimes, you actually hit upon the truth.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:57.110
But, you know, she's the type of person who's
unable to get married... she's too anxious. Ooh-ah!

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:57.650
Hey!

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:00.410
First, he compliments me and then, he tears me down...

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:06.540
You know, when it comes to dogs, both males
and females are responsible for providing food.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:10.210
As for foxes, when they're raising kits,
it's the male who prepares the food.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:13.000
With lions, it's the female who takes care of all that, right?

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:15.800
So shouldn't it be fine... no matter how you handle it?

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:17.170
That's right...

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.800
In the first place, Miki, you're a yakan, right?

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:25.350
I feel like we're straying quite far from the point at issue...
this presents a purroblem for my image.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.180
Ah, I get it!

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:31.230
Miki, you're terrified of the cooking segment
on the new TV show we'll be appearing in.

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:31.690
Meow!

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:33.440
"New TV show"?

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:36.570
The idea is that Maki-Miki
will be attempting lots of new things...

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:39.490
Well, it's one of those pop-idol shows
they often have late at night.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:42.240
Ah, those shows always do have something like that...

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:44.160
A homemade-bento segment, for example.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:48.200
But, it's actually more appealing from
a programming standpoint if the bento looks really bad.

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:49.540
I WON'T HAVE IT, MEOW!

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:52.790
I can't cause my parents any more grief, meow!

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:57.920
Additionally, even before considering the flavor,
I think this bento is in poor taste.

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:00.380
This one's just meant for my blog!

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:04.140
I see. I'll check it out later...
and see if you're getting a flood of criticism.

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:07.640
Alright, alright, I guess I have no choice...

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:10.350
I'll teach you! For the sake of Maki-Miki!

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:14.190
Beef
Pork
Chicken

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:14.310
First, get some beef, pork, and chicken ready.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.980
Parboil it a bit, and you're done!

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:21.030
Got it? Easy, right?

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:24.160
Thanks...

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:27.330
Fine, then, I'll teach you.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:31.910
First, get the surplus heads of the deceased
that any household should have in their refrigerator...

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:31.790
Beer
Mucchin Pudding
(Papa)
Bamboo Shoots
Lettuce                   Wheat

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:33.830
I don't have any surplus dead, meow!

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.960
Next time, try using a normal refrigerator!

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:38.460
Well then, take a really fresh spiny lobster...

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.170
We don't have spiny lobster either!

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:43.090
Mr. Hozuki, do you actually cook regularly?!

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:44.970
I do not.

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:46.090
Just as I thought!

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:51.980
Throwing something together day after day and
making an ornate meal once in a while are not the same!

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:54.980
"I regularly cook" and
"I'm able to cook" are different things.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:53.480
I
regularly

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:53.480
cook

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:54.850
I
regularly
cook
I'm able
to cook

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:55.650
DIFFERENT THINGS
I
regularly
cook

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:55.650
I'm able
to cook

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:59.150
Perhaps I am overly fanatical.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:01.780
It did take me 10 years to make sushi, after all.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:04.070
You can make sushi, Mr. Hozuki?!

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:06.490
Next time I catch a tuna,
will you make sushi with it for me?!

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:09.830
Leaving that aside, I'm in a real jam here right meow!

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:13.210
If my manager finds out about this,
I'm not sure how he might try to leverage it!

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:16.580
Miki, so you're not good at cooking.
Yeah, okay, makes sense.

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:17.670
GAAAAAAH!

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:19.130
THAT DEVIL'S HERE!

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:21.460
That guy thinks of us as mere things!

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:25.630
Yep, right, I don't think of you girls
as anything other than a product.

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:31.560
This makes for good material, but packing too much
into your persona's no good, so let's hold off for a bit.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:33.930
Miki...

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:39.820
Absolutely do not get good at cooking...
if you have any awareness as an entertainer, that is.

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:45.860
A kid...

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:46.950
Hm?

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:50.120
MAYBE I'LL JUST HAVE ONE OF THOSE!
AN ILLEGITIMATE ONE!

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:54.160
I'll always be a fan of yours no matter what! Do your best!

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:10.760
Uso yo. Janakya naze koko ni tadoritsuku no?
That's a lie. If not, why do you find your way here?

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:17.350
Enma-sama no mae de nao shira o kiru no ne
Even in front of Lord Enma, you feign ignorance

00:22:17.810 --> 00:22:23.280
Baka ne. Dakedo sonna toko tamaranakute
You're an idiot. But I can't get enough of that aspect of you

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:29.660
Teitaraku. Onaji tsumi kasanetsuzuketa
What a predicament. You continued to repeat the same sin

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:34.950
Ii no? Yubikiri genman.
Is that alright? Pinky swear.

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:36.330
(E?)
(Huh?)
Ii no? Yubikiri genman.
Is that alright? Pinky swear.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:41.170
Gachi ni honto ni naru yo.
It will seriously become reality.

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:42.750
(Dogii!)
(Startling!)

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:42.750
Gachi ni honto ni naru yo.
It will seriously become reality.

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:49.130
Tensei o matazu shounetsu no mama ni
Without waiting for reincarnation, while still in the scorching heat

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:55.180
Asa hiru eien ai o kushizashi narabete
Morning, midday, and eternally skewer desires and line them up

00:22:55.430 --> 00:22:58.350
Gutsu gutsu mou! Nie nie da yo
Already simmering! It's boiling

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:01.770
Yuuge wa jigoku de hot pot
Supper is a hot pot in Hell

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:07.990
Nita mono doushi ni oniai no oshioki
For people who are alike, a suitable punishment

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:11.110
Juu juu achi! Koge koge da yo
Sizzling hot! It's burned to a crisp

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:14.410
Anata to jigoku de hotcake
Hotcakes with you in Hell

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:19.830
Tokoyo no suna ni naru made
Until they become forever-unchanging sand

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:26.800
NEXT TIME
ON HOZUKI'S
COOLHEADEDNESS...

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:29.760
Achoo! I phink baybe I caught a cold...

00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:28.630
AND

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:33.600
Okapi, pygmy hippo, Iriomote cat,
Okinawa rail, kiwi, panda, baby panda.

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:31.760
BUT

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:34.470
SO

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:36.220
Huh? What's the matter, Hozuki? You alive?

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:39.230
I'm dead. You and I are both dead.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.730
WE PRESENT:
ONKI
AND
ANIMALS DON'T FORGET
ONE'S KINDNESS

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.730
PLEASE ENJOY!
